course: dictionary
lesson: 5142
title: IOU: a note for money owed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An IOU is a short written note that says you owe someone money. Its name is a shortcut: the letters I, O and U sound like the words «I owe you».
explain: «To lend is to let someone use your money for a while; an IOU, short for "I owe you", is a note saying someone owes money.» Lend means let someone use your money for a while, and the IOU is the note that shows the debt.
explain: IOU can also be used informally for a promise to do something or pay back later. Look at the words around it to tell which meaning the writer means.
fact: IOU is an abbreviation, a short form of "I owe you".
fact: An IOU is a noun: you can write an IOU, or give someone an IOU.
fact: «IOU for £5» means a note showing that £5 is owed.
fact: Informally, an IOU can mean a promise to do something or pay back later.
fact: Money words like lend and owe are useful to know: lend means let someone use your money for a while, and owe means you must pay someone back.
exercise: What does the abbreviation IOU stand for? | "Input orders urgently" | "I only use" | *"I owe you" | "I own you"
exercise: Ravi writes «IOU £2» on a slip of paper. What does the note show? | Ravi has already paid £2 and nothing is owed | Ravi is giving away £2 as a present | Ravi has found £2 on the ground | *Ravi owes someone £2
exercise: «To lend is to let someone use your money for a while.» What does lend mean? | To count coins | *To let someone use your money for a while | To keep money safe in a box | To spend money on sweets
test: Which of these is the informal meaning of IOU? | Writing a note about a broken window | *A promise to do something or pay back later | A shop that sells sweets | A kind of coin
test: «An IOU for £5» shows what? | Someone has spent £5 and nothing is owed | A prize of £5 | *Someone owes £5 | A £5 coin
exam: Ella gives Sam an IOU for her pocket money. What does Sam know? | Sam has lost his pocket money | *Ella must pay Sam back later | Ella has already paid Sam | Sam must pay Ella back
